Type of growth: new product for current market—it is clear who to sell to and through which channels.

Decisions before the date:
who gets it first—40 clients with more than 20 counterparties; it hurts them;
what we promise—"reconciliation in an hour instead of a day", not "a new module";
how we sell—inside the product to those who open the counterparty list;
price—included in the current plan for a quarter, then separate;
support—two people trained in advance, answers ready for three expected questions;
success—25% of 40 used it within a month and half of them repeated.

The announcement date turned out to be the least important of these decisions.
